            "especially",
            "robotics",
            "those",
            "resets",
            "expensive",
            "requiring",
            "human",
            "supervision"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c3_jin_kim_seoul_national_university",
          "text": "Jin Kim from Seoul National University, tackles autonomous reinforcement learning without any resets and, crucially, without any demonstrations. Their method, called IBC, combines an auxiliary agent that fades away as the main agent improves with a bidirectional goal curriculum built on optimal transport.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "jin",
            "kim",
            "seoul",
            "national",
            "university",
            "tackles",
            "autonomous",
            "reinforcement",
            "learning",
            "without"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c4_result_state_of_the_art_performance",
          "text": "The result is state-of-the-art performance on non-episodic benchmarks, matching methods that rely on expert data and even approaching episodic oracle reinforcement learning.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "result",
            "state-of-the-art",
            "performance",
            "non-episodic",
            "benchmarks",
            "matching",
            "methods",
            "rely",
            "expert",
            "even"
          ],
          "required": true
